{"game": "aliens-fireteam-elite", "language": "english", "appid": 1549970, "month": "2022-07", "window": 1, "start_date": 1656633600, "end_date": 1657238399, "month_true_total": 339, "quota": 6, "returned": 6, "pulled_at": "2026-09-04 02:20:43 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "118419242", "author": {"steamid": "76561198087496299", "personaname": "Partizani", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198087496299/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 2973, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 540, "last_played": 1722834112, "avatar": "a2d0f2481294823e64c0c6aa290a987e76950826"}, "language": "english", "review": "Hall way shooter that has friendly fire but no way to minimize yourself from friendly fire i.e. crouching, leaning, other than it's (albeit) worse version of a 'gears of war' like cover system with only a few surfaces here and there that are good positions to crouch down behind which is only compounded by the lack of the most basic form of communication, the text message box. Pings and that's It. Not even a wheel with dialogue options for the most basic of things like \"Need Healing\" \"Out of Ammo\" or even \"Group up\" Nothing. You need a group of people with mics and third party application to coordinate If you want to have fun, otherwise you'll get randoms 2-300 levels below the recommended combat rating constantly shooting you in the back and refusing to heal themselves or use their class abilities to heal others and abandoning as soon as they go downed. \n\nEDIT: Upon reading other reviews, I've learned the developers lied about free content expansions and only cosmetic stuff would have to be bought and then tried to cover that up, so don't even give them a penny, especially lacking all the quality-of-life elements It sorely needs. It's a shameless glorified MOBILE SHOOTER that an't even worth 20$", "timestamp_created": 1657237951, "timestamp_upda